<report>
<line><title>Sample size for <in>tt</in> Student t test</title></line>
<line></line>
<line>Alpha = <in>alpha</in></line>
<line>Power = <in>power</in></line>
<line>Difference <in>mean</in> = <in>delta</in></line>
<line>Standard deviation = <in>sd</in></line>
<block name="controls"><line>Controls per experimental subject <in>con_per</in></line></block>
<line></line>
<line>Estimated minimum sample size = <in>size</in> <block name="pairs">pairs</block><block name="subjects"> experimental subjects and <in>con_tot</in> controls.</block></line>
<line></line>
<line>Degrees of freedom = <in>df</in></line>
<block name="assumptions">
<line></line>
<line>NB:Assumptions of this calculation may cause over estimation of sample size when power is low.</line>
<line>However, true power associated with <in>cases</in> cases will be no less than <in>no_less</in> and no greater than <in>no_greater</in>.</line>
</block>
</report>
